; caps_base.writ — a model whose element names are ALL-CAPS.
;
; This checks clean as a .writ file: the kernel has no opinion about case. But a
; .rules file reads an ALL-CAPS atom as a VARIABLE (extension §9), and quoting is
; no escape because the reader returns the same atom either way — so `KNIGHT`
; written in a rule would be silently misread. Extension §3 diagnoses the
; collision at the atom instead; caps_collision.rules is the file that trips it.

(schema caps
  (type kind-t (KNIGHT KNAVE))
  (type islander
    (arrow kind (to kind-t) fixed)
    (arrow says (to kind-t))))

(instance camp caps
  (islander alice (kind KNIGHT)
                  (says KNIGHT))
  (islander bob (kind KNAVE)
                (says KNIGHT)))

(use caps)
(initial camp)

(transition bob-recants
  (when (is bob.says KNIGHT))
  (do (set bob.says KNAVE)))
